<h2>Introduction to Computer Systems</h2>
<h3>What Is a Computer System?</h3>
<p>
                    A computer system is an electronic system
                    that receives data, processes information,
                    stores files, and produces useful results.
                </p>
<p>
                    It is made up of different components that
                    work together to perform tasks. These
                    components include hardware, software,
                    memory, storage devices, and other
                    important parts.
                </p>
<p>
                    Computers are widely used in schools,
                    offices, businesses, hospitals, government
                    agencies, and homes. They help people
                    complete tasks faster, communicate with
                    others, organize information, and solve
                    different problems.
                </p>
<h3>Four Basic Operations of a Computer System</h3>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Input:</strong>
                        The computer receives data from the user
                        through devices such as a keyboard,
                        mouse, or microphone.
                    </li>
<li>
<strong>Processing:</strong>
                        The processor works on information
                        based on the instructions given.
                    </li>
<li>
<strong>Output:</strong>
                        The computer presents processed
                        information through a monitor,
                        printer, or speaker.
                    </li>
<li>
<strong>Storage:</strong>
                        The computer saves information so
                        it can be accessed again in the future.
                    </li>
</ol>
<div class="example-box">
<h3>Example: Creating a Document</h3>
<ul>
<li>
                            The student types information
                            using a keyboard.
                        </li>
<li>
                            The CPU processes the instructions.
                        </li>
<li>
                            The monitor displays the document.
                        </li>
<li>
                            The storage device saves the file
                            for future use.
                        </li>
</ul>
</div>
<h3>Importance of Computer Systems</h3>
<p>
                    Computer systems make everyday activities
                    more convenient and efficient. They allow
                    users to perform calculations, create
                    documents, manage records, communicate
                    online, and access information.
                </p>
<p>
                    They also support modern technologies
                    such as artificial intelligence, online
                    education, digital banking, and
                    scientific research.
                </p>
</section>
