<h2>Meaning of Computer System Platforms</h2>
<h3>What Is a Computer System Platform?</h3>
<p>
                    A computer system platform refers to the
                    combination of hardware and software that
                    allows a computer or digital device to
                    operate and run applications.
                </p>
<p>
                    A platform provides the environment where
                    programs are installed and executed. It
                    includes the processor, memory, operating
                    system, and other technologies needed
                    to support computer operations.
                </p>
<div class="example-box">
<h3>Examples</h3>
<p>
                        A desktop computer with an Intel
                        processor and Windows operating
                        system is one type of computer platform.
                    </p>
<p>
                        A smartphone using an ARM-based
                        processor and Android is another
                        type of computer platform.
                    </p>
</div>
<h3>Main Elements of a Computer Platform</h3>
<h3>1. Hardware</h3>
<p>
                    Hardware refers to the physical components
                    of a computer. These are the parts that
                    users can physically see and touch.
                </p>
<ul>
<li>Monitor</li>
<li>Keyboard</li>
<li>Mouse</li>
<li>CPU</li>
<li>RAM</li>
<li>Hard drive</li>
</ul>
<h3>2. Software</h3>
<p>
                    Software refers to the programs and
                    instructions that tell the computer
                    what to do.
                </p>
<ul>
<li>Windows</li>
<li>Linux</li>
<li>Android</li>
<li>Microsoft Word</li>
<li>Google Chrome</li>
</ul>
<h3>3. Operating System</h3>
<p>
                    The operating system manages the computer's
                    hardware and software resources. It allows
                    users to interact with the computer and
                    run different applications.
                </p>
<h3>4. Processor Architecture</h3>
<p>
                    Processor architecture describes how a
                    processor is designed and how it handles
                    instructions and data.
                </p>
<div class="example-box">
<h3>Example: Laptop Platform</h3>
<ul>
<li>Intel Core processor</li>
<li>8 GB RAM</li>
<li>512 GB SSD</li>
<li>Windows operating system</li>
</ul>
<p>
                        These components work together to
                        create a computer platform that
                        supports web browsers, programming
                        tools, and office software.
                    </p>
</div>
<h3>Why Are Platforms Important?</h3>
<p>
                    Computer platforms provide the foundation
                    for applications to function. Without a
                    compatible platform, certain programs
                    may not work properly or may not run at all.
                </p>
</section>
