<h2>Meaning of Computer Architecture</h2>
<h3>What Is Computer Architecture?</h3>
<p>
                    Computer architecture refers to the design
                    and organization of a computer system.
                    It explains how the different parts of a
                    computer are arranged and how they
                    communicate with each other to perform tasks.
                </p>
<p>
                    It focuses on how the processor works,
                    how memory stores information, how
                    instructions are executed, and how data
                    moves between components.
                </p>
<p>
                    Computer architecture serves as a guide
                    for understanding how a computer
                    operates internally.
                </p>
<h3>Main Elements of Computer Architecture</h3>
<ol>
<li>
<strong>Instruction Set Architecture (ISA)</strong>
<p>
                            Defines the instructions that a
                            processor can understand and execute.
                            It acts as a connection between
                            software and hardware.
                        </p>
<p>
                            Examples include x86-64 and ARM.
                        </p>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Processor Design</strong>
<p>
                            Explains how the CPU is organized
                            and how it performs operations.
                        </p>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Memory Organization</strong>
<p>
                            Describes how data and instructions
                            are stored and accessed by
                            the computer.
                        </p>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Input and Output Organization</strong>
<p>
                            Explains how a computer receives
                            information and sends results
                            to external devices.
                        </p>
</li>
<li>
<strong>Data Communication</strong>
<p>
                            Describes how different computer
                            components exchange information
                            through buses and other connections.
                        </p>
</li>
</ol>
<div class="example-box">
<h3>Example: Opening a Web Browser</h3>
<p>
                        When a user opens a web browser,
                        the operating system sends instructions
                        to the processor.
                    </p>
<p>
                        The CPU processes those instructions,
                        memory holds the information currently
                        being used, and the display presents
                        the browser window.
                    </p>
</div>
<h3>Importance of Computer Architecture</h3>
<p>
                    Understanding computer architecture helps
                    IT students learn how computers work
                    internally. It is also useful when
                    studying programming, computer hardware,
                    operating systems, and troubleshooting.
                </p>
</section>
