<section class="chapter" id="page-14">
<span class="chapter-number">LESSON 14</span>
<h2>Motherboard and System Bus</h2>
<h3>What Is a Motherboard?</h3>
<p>
                    The motherboard is the main circuit
                    board of a computer.
                </p>
<p>
                    It provides the connections that allow
                    different hardware components to
                    communicate and work together.
                </p>
<p>
                    It contains slots, connectors, circuits,
                    and other features that support
                    computer operations.
                </p>
<h3>Main Parts of a Motherboard</h3>
<h3>1. CPU Socket</h3>
<p>
                    The CPU socket is the location
                    where the processor is installed.
                </p>
<h3>2. RAM Slots</h3>
