<h2>Performance and System Specifications</h2>
<h3>What Is Computer Performance?</h3>
<p>
                    Computer performance refers to how
                    efficiently a computer system completes tasks.
                </p>
<p>
                    It depends on several hardware
                    and software factors.
                </p>
<p>
                    A computer with suitable specifications
                    can run applications more smoothly
                    and handle demanding workloads.
                </p>
<h3>Important Performance Factors</h3>
<h3>1. Processor Speed</h3>
<p>
                    The CPU's clock speed is measured in hertz,
                    commonly gigahertz.
                </p>
<p>
                    It indicates the frequency at which
                    the processor operates.
                </p>
<h3>2. Number of CPU Cores</h3>
<p>
                    More cores can help a computer handle
                    multiple processing tasks, depending
                    on the application and workload.
                </p>
<h3>3. RAM Capacity</h3>
<p>
                    More RAM allows a system to keep more
                    active programs and data in memory.
                </p>
<h3>4. Storage Performance</h3>
<p>
                    SSDs generally provide faster file
                    access and system startup than
                    traditional HDDs.
                </p>
<h3>5. Graphics Processing</h3>
<p>
                    A GPU improves graphics performance
                    and supports workloads such as
                    video editing, 3D rendering,
                    and certain scientific tasks.
                </p>
<h3>6. Cooling System</h3>
<p>
                    Cooling systems help maintain suitable
                    operating temperatures and reduce
                    the risk of performance problems
                    caused by overheating.
                </p>
<div class="example-box">
<h3>Example</h3>
<p>
                        A computer with a modern processor,
                        sufficient RAM, and an SSD may
                        load applications faster and handle
                        multiple tasks more smoothly than
                        an older system with limited memory
                        and a slower hard drive.
                    </p>
</div>
<h3>Importance</h3>
<p>
                    Understanding specifications helps users
                    select computers based on their needs,
                    such as schoolwork, programming,
                    graphic design, gaming, and
                    business operations.
                </p>
</section>
