<h2>Computer Security and Reliability</h2>
<h3>What Is Computer Security?</h3>
<p>
                    Computer security refers to the methods
                    and technologies used to protect computer
                    systems, information, and networks from
                    unauthorized access, damage, and other
                    digital threats.
                </p>
<p>
                    Security is important because computers
                    often store personal information, school
                    records, business documents, and other
                    valuable data.
                </p>
<h3>Common Security Practices</h3>
<h3>1. Strong Passwords</h3>
<p>
                    Users should create unique passwords
                    that are difficult to guess.
                </p>
<h3>2. Software Updates</h3>
<p>
                    Installing updates helps maintain system
                    stability and addresses known security
                    weaknesses.
                </p>
<h3>3. Antivirus Protection</h3>
<p>
                    Security software can help detect and
                    respond to malicious programs.
                </p>
<h3>4. Data Backup</h3>
<p>
                    Backing up files helps users recover
                    information if the original files
                    are lost or damaged.
                </p>
<h3>5. Access Control</h3>
<p>
                    Access control limits system resources
                    to authorized users.
                </p>
<h3>6. Network Security</h3>
<p>
                    Security measures help protect information
                    exchanged through computer networks.
                </p>
<h3>What Is Computer Reliability?</h3>
<p>
                    Reliability refers to the ability of
                    a computer system to operate correctly
                    and consistently over time.
                </p>
<h3>Factors That Affect Reliability</h3>
<ul>
<li>Quality of hardware components.</li>
<li>Proper cooling and ventilation.</li>
<li>Regular system maintenance.</li>
<li>Stable power supply.</li>
<li>Correct software installation.</li>
<li>Data protection and backup procedures.</li>
</ul>
<div class="example-box">
<h3>Example</h3>
<p>
                        A school computer laboratory can
                        improve reliability by maintaining
                        computers, updating software,
                        checking hardware, and keeping
                        backup copies of important school files.
                    </p>
</div>
<h3>Importance</h3>
<p>
                    Computer security protects information,
                    while reliability helps ensure that
                    systems remain available and perform
                    their intended tasks.
                </p>
</section>
